# This repo tracks only my own work + tooling, never teacher-posted
# course materials -- see README.md. Everything below is belt-and-
# braces; the actual staging uses explicit `git add` on specific paths,
# not `git add -A`, so this mainly guards against future mistakes.

# secrets
classroom_tool/credentials.json
classroom_tool/token.json
phase1_auth_spike/credentials.json
phase1_auth_spike/token.json

# venvs
**/venv/

# NOTE: deliberately NOT blanket-ignoring the semester folders here.
# Git's directory-level ignore blocks descending into the directory at
# all, which would fight with the explicit `git add` of specific
# my-submission/ and README.md paths inside them (would need `add -f`
# everywhere). Scoping to "my own work only" is enforced entirely by
# what gets explicitly `git add`-ed (see the batch commit commands),
# never by `git add -A` / `git add .`. Everything else under Fall*/
# Spring*/Summer*/ just shows as untracked in `git status` and is
# never staged.

# partial/in-progress downloads
*.part

# scratch
classroom_tool/download_failures.log
classroom_tool/*.test.yaml
__pycache__/
.claude/
